<node id="F003">
  <data key="d2">In-line assistance - when is it more useful?</data>
  <data key="d3">practitioner_essay</data>
  <data key="d4">F</data>
  <data key="d5">Birgitta Böckeler</data>
  <data key="d6">["Birgitta Böckeler"]</data>
  <data key="d7">2023-08-01</data>
  <data key="d8">Dated entry on the supplied series index; article date also used where printed</data>
  <data key="d9">https://martinfowler.com/articles/exploring-gen-ai/03-coding-assistance-when-useful.html</data>
  <data key="d10">martinfowler.com</data>
  <data key="d11">Exploring Generative AI</data>
  <data key="d12">https://martinfowler.com/articles/exploring-gen-ai.html</data>
  <data key="d13">2026-10-13</data>
  <data key="d14">Discusses when inline suggestions help, considering task familiarity, technology, change size, developer experience and the effort of checking or reworking the output.</data>
  <data key="d15">Experience-based guidance, largely from experienced developers; usefulness is not a measured universal productivity effect.</data>
  <data key="d16">Practitioner experience</data>
  <data key="d17">Body: usefulness factors and review/rework effort</data>
