<node id="F004">
  <data key="d2">In-line assistance - how can it get in the way?</data>
  <data key="d3">practitioner_essay</data>
  <data key="d4">F</data>
  <data key="d5">Birgitta Böckeler</data>
  <data key="d6">["Birgitta Böckeler"]</data>
  <data key="d7">2023-08-03</data>
  <data key="d8">Dated entry on the supplied series index; article date also used where printed</data>
  <data key="d9">https://martinfowler.com/articles/exploring-gen-ai/04-coding-assistance-how-in-the-way.html</data>
  <data key="d10">martinfowler.com</data>
  <data key="d11">Exploring Generative AI</data>
  <data key="d12">https://martinfowler.com/articles/exploring-gen-ai.html</data>
  <data key="d13">2026-10-13</data>
  <data key="d14">Describes assistants repeating poor patterns from their context and the burden of continually judging suggestions. Relates these experiences to automation bias, anchoring and reluctance to discard generated work.</data>
  <data key="d15">Qualitative examples and interpretive mechanisms, not measured frequencies of bias or review fatigue.</data>
  <data key="d16">Practitioner experience</data>
  <data key="d17">Body: reinforcing existing practices; reviewing instead of producing</data>
