<node id="F005">
  <data key="d2">Coding assistants do not replace pair programming</data>
  <data key="d3">practitioner_essay</data>
  <data key="d4">F</data>
  <data key="d5">Birgitta Böckeler</data>
  <data key="d6">["Birgitta Böckeler"]</data>
  <data key="d7">2023-08-10</data>
  <data key="d8">Dated entry on the supplied series index; article date also used where printed</data>
  <data key="d9">https://martinfowler.com/articles/exploring-gen-ai/05-not-your-pair-programmer.html</data>
  <data key="d10">martinfowler.com</data>
  <data key="d11">Exploring Generative AI</data>
  <data key="d12">https://martinfowler.com/articles/exploring-gen-ai.html</data>
  <data key="d13">2026-10-13</data>
  <data key="d14">Argues that code assistance does not replace the human knowledge sharing, collaboration and collective understanding associated with pair programming. Tools can instead be used by a human pair.</data>
  <data key="d15">An argument about the functions of pairing; not a controlled comparison of pairing arrangements.</data>
  <data key="d16">Conceptual argument</data>
  <data key="d17">Body: knowledge sharing, team flow and pairing with assistance</data>
