<node id="F007">
  <data key="d2">How is GenAI different from other code generators?</data>
  <data key="d3">practitioner_essay</data>
  <data key="d4">F</data>
  <data key="d5">Birgitta Böckeler</data>
  <data key="d6">["Birgitta Böckeler"]</data>
  <data key="d7">2023-09-19</data>
  <data key="d8">Dated entry on the supplied series index; article date also used where printed</data>
  <data key="d9">https://martinfowler.com/articles/exploring-gen-ai/07-how-is-this-different.html</data>
  <data key="d10">martinfowler.com</data>
  <data key="d11">Exploring Generative AI</data>
  <data key="d12">https://martinfowler.com/articles/exploring-gen-ai.html</data>
  <data key="d13">2026-10-13</data>
  <data key="d14">Contrasts generative assistance with model-driven development and domain-specific code generators. Examines how control and abstraction differ when generation draws on broad learned patterns rather than an explicitly designed transformation.</data>
  <data key="d15">Conceptual comparison; it does not demonstrate the reliability or economic superiority of either approach.</data>
  <data key="d16">Conceptual argument</data>
  <data key="d17">Body: abstraction levels and comparison with traditional generation</data>
  <data key="d18">Primary article byline and selected body passages inspected; no independent execution or statistical replication</data>
