<node id="F008">
  <data key="d2">How to tackle unreliability of coding assistants</data>
  <data key="d3">practitioner_essay</data>
  <data key="d4">F</data>
  <data key="d5">Birgitta Böckeler</data>
  <data key="d6">["Birgitta Böckeler"]</data>
  <data key="d7">2023-11-29</data>
  <data key="d8">Dated entry on the supplied series index; article date also used where printed</data>
  <data key="d9">https://martinfowler.com/articles/exploring-gen-ai/08-how-to-tackle-unreliability.html</data>
  <data key="d10">martinfowler.com</data>
  <data key="d11">Exploring Generative AI</data>
  <data key="d12">https://martinfowler.com/articles/exploring-gen-ai.html</data>
  <data key="d13">2026-10-13</data>
  <data key="d14">Frames confidence in assistance around feedback, the developer’s ability to check an answer and the consequences of error. Proposes timeboxing unproductive assistance and retaining responsibility for the result.</data>
  <data key="d15">Personal heuristics rather than calibrated reliability estimates; informal numerical intuitions are not treated as measured rates.</data>
  <data key="d16">Practitioner guidance</data>
  <data key="d17">Body: confidence, timeboxing and assistant persona</data>
